From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: sky1: strap host-only controllers as host

Sky1 has one Type-C DRD controller and nine host-only controllers. The
wrapper currently programs every controller's S5 mode strap as OTG during
drd_init(), including the host-only Type-C, Type-A and USB2 instances.

That leaves Linux with xHCI root hubs but the SoC-side port logic is not
forced into host mode, so downstream devices do not connect. Keep OTG only
for U3_TYPEC_DRD_ID and program every other controller as HOST.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific]
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
index 8483e7532eb8..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
@@ -283,6 +283,7 @@ static int cdnsp_sky1_drd_init(struct cdnsp_sky1 *data)
 	int ret;
 	int clk;
 	int v0, v1, v2;
+	int mode;
 
 	reset_control_assert(data->reset);
 	reset_control_assert(data->preset);
@@ -291,7 +292,15 @@ static int cdnsp_sky1_drd_init(struct cdnsp_sky1 *data)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 	writel(CIX_USB_AXI_WR_CACHE_VALUE, data->axi_base);
-	sky1_set_mode_by_id(data->dev, MODE_STRAP_OTG);
+
+	/*
+	 * Only controller 0 is a real DRD port. All other Sky1 USBSSP
+	 * instances are host-only, so force their S5 mode straps to HOST.
+	 */
+	mode = data->id == U3_TYPEC_DRD_ID ? MODE_STRAP_OTG : MODE_STRAP_HOST;
+	ret = sky1_set_mode_by_id(data->dev, mode);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 	reset_control_deassert(data->preset);
 	if (data->u3_disable) {
 		dev_info(data->dev, "[%s:%d]disable u3 port\n", __func__, __LINE__);
-- 
